---
// The per-frame handshake between the guest vCPU and the host event loop.
// The guest draws, rings a port-IO doorbell that exits to the host, and parks;
// the host blits the framebuffer, writes input into the mailbox, and resumes
// the guest. Static SVG, themed by the shared figure.diagram CSS.
---

<figure class="diagram doorbell">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 410" role="img"
    aria-label="Each frame: the guest draws into the framebuffer and writes to the frame port, which exits to the host. The host blits the framebuffer to the window and writes the latest input and time into the mailbox, then resumes the guest for the next frame.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="db-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <text class="db-tag" x="150" y="26">guest vCPU thread</text>
    <text class="db-tag" x="490" y="26">host event loop</text>
    <line class="db-divider" x1="320" y1="40" x2="320" y2="374" />

    <!-- guest draws -->
    <g class="node">
      <rect class="box" x="40" y="52" width="220" height="46" rx="9" />
      <text class="box-label" x="150" y="75">draw frame into framebuffer</text>
    </g>
    <!-- doorbell: down out of the guest box, across, down into the host box -->
    <path class="edge" d="M 150 98 V 140 H 490 V 164" marker-end="url(#db-arrow)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="325" y="132" text-anchor="middle">out to frame port · vCPU exits</text>

    <!-- host work -->
    <g class="node">
      <rect class="box" x="380" y="170" width="220" height="46" rx="9" />
      <text class="box-label" x="490" y="193">blit to window</text>
    </g>
    <line class="edge" x1="490" y1="216" x2="490" y2="230" marker-end="url(#db-arrow)" />
    <g class="node">
      <rect class="box" x="380" y="236" width="220" height="46" rx="9" />
      <text class="box-label" x="490" y="259">write input + time to mailbox</text>
    </g>

    <!-- resume: down out of the host box, across, down into the guest box -->
    <path class="edge" d="M 490 282 V 324 H 150 V 348" marker-end="url(#db-arrow)" />
    <text class="edge-label" x="325" y="316" text-anchor="middle">resume · next frame</text>
    <g class="node">
      <rect class="box" x="40" y="354" width="220" height="40" rx="9" />
      <text class="box-label" x="150" y="375">read mailbox, apply input</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>The guest is stopped the whole time the host touches shared memory, so the mailbox needs no lock. One port write per frame is the entire protocol.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  figure.doorbell .db-tag {
    fill: var(--fg); font: 600 13px ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; text-anchor: middle;
  }
  figure.doorbell .db-divider { stroke: var(--rule); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }
</style>
